.TH qsh-init 1  "init 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-init \- Create this device\*(Aqs identity (keypair + self\-signed certificate). Idempotent: re\-running reports the existing identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh init\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-store\fR] [\fB\-\-import\-ssh\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create this device\*(Aqs identity (keypair + self\-signed certificate). Idempotent: re\-running reports the existing identity
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-store\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Where to keep the private key: `auto` (platform store, falling back to a 0600 file), `platform` or `file`. Defaults to `config.toml`\*(Aqs `[identity].key_store`, then `auto`
.TP
\fB\-\-import\-ssh\-key\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use this plaintext OpenSSH Ed25519 private key as the device key instead of generating one (ADR\-0026). Only valid before an identity exists; prints the qsh and the SSH fingerprint side by side. Nothing is pinned and `acl.toml` is never written
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR
When the ssh bootstrap finds no `qsh` on the remote host (or one too old to answer it), install this machine\*(Aqs release into `~/.local/bin` there without asking (`docs/CLI.md` §7). Works with `\-\-json`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR
Never install or upgrade `qsh` on the remote host, and do not ask; a missing `qsh` ends as `remote_qsh_missing`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
